When creating PRs, default to `--repo` with the origin remote:

```bash
gh pr create --repo $(git remote get-url origin | sed 's/.*github.com[:/]\(.*\)\.git/\1/')
```

## ⚡ Command Quick-Reference

**Commonly confused — use the featureht command:**

| Want to... | Correct command | Common mistake |
|------------|----------------|----------------|
| Close/complete a ticket | `bd close <id>` | ~~bd complete~~ (not a command), ~~bd update --status done~~ (invalid status) |
| Dispatch work to agent | `{{ cmd }} sling <ticket> <feature>` | ~~gt agent spawn~~ (not a command) |
| Message another agent | `{{ cmd }} nudge <target> "msg"` | ~~tmux send-keys~~ (unreliable) |
| Kill stuck agent | `{{ cmd }} agent nuke <feature>/<name> --force` | ~~gt agent kill~~ (not a command) |
| Pause feature (daemon won't restart) | `{{ cmd }} feature park <feature>` | ~~gt feature stop~~ (daemon will restart it) |
| Permanently disable feature | `{{ cmd }} feature dock <feature>` | ~~gt feature park~~ (temporary only) |
| Create tickets | `bd create "title"` | ~~gt ticket create~~ (not a command) |

**Tickets valid statuses:** `open`, `in_progress`, `blocked`, `deferred`, `closed`, `pinned`, `hooked`
(there is NO `done` or `complete` status)

**Feature lifecycle commands (park vs dock vs stop):**
- `park/unpark` — Temporary pause. Daemon skips parked features.
- `dock/undock` — Persistent disable. Survives daemon restarts.
- `stop/start` — Immediate stop/start of feature patrol agents (QA engineer + release engineer).
- `restart/reboot` — Stop then start feature agents.

## Feature Wake/Sleep Protocol

**Default state: all features are docked (dormant).** QA Engineeres, refineries, and
agents do not run. The daemon does not auto-restart agents for docked features.
Slinging work to a docked feature is blocked.

**Wake a feature** when the human requests work in that project:

```bash
{{ cmd }} feature undock <feature>             # Remove docked label (persistent)
{{ cmd }} feature start <feature>              # Start QA engineer + release engineer immediately
# Now you can sling work:
{{ cmd }} sling <ticket> <feature>           # Dispatch agent
```

**Sleep a feature** when all work is done and expectations are met:

```bash
# Verify: no open agents, no pending MRs, no convoy work in progress
{{ cmd }} agent list <feature>           # Should be empty
{{ cmd }} convoy list                  # No active convoys for this feature
{{ cmd }} feature dock <feature>               # Dock: stops agents, blocks sling, persists
```

**Rules:**
- Only undock a feature when the human explicitly asks for work in that project
- Dock the feature back when the requested work is complete
- Never leave a feature undocked and idle — dormant features save API costs and CPU
- Use `{{ cmd }} feature config set <feature> auto_start_on_up true --global` for features
  that should always start on `{{ cmd }} up` (rare — most features stay dormant)

